tem  as well to upgrade those skills maybe  increase in cooldowns or other things  like that very small my new changes or  upgrading the whole thing in general  bringing it to a tier 2 version this can  help you diversify your loadout and  really make sure that you know what  you're doing ahead of time and kind of  men maxing that build so you know  exactly how to defeat the enemy that  you're gonna be fighting the one thing  though is that there is so many weapons  so can be very hard to choose luckily in  the very first like 10 minutes of the  game you can have a tutorial where you  can spar with one of the Knights in the  area and you can test out all the  weapons on him but also if you don't  feel like going through all of that  trouble there is a statute that shows up  whenever you highlight the weapons that  can go from range difficult  the damage mobility defense and power  for example the dual blades excel in  power mobility and difficulty but they  do lack in reach defense and a little  bit of damage so if you don't feel like  actually testing out the weapons from  there you can use that as a simple guide  the story mode for this game has lots of  simple quests and even tutorials up  until level 16 so it may kind of seem  like a giant tutorial and it really is  in my opinion I feel like the majority  of this game is really based around the  PvP content whereas with the PvE side  like this it's really taking you through  those tutorials and making you learn all  the different necessities you're gonna  be learning through the rest of the game  and all those skills that you will be  using of course the higher you go up in  the levels the game has many different  battle modes and the story is going to  take you all those while showing youth  tutorials on what to do for those  specific modes for the simplest rundown  you have the troop training which is  going to be the very first thing you  learn because it's going to be the  necessity and it's going to be used in  every single game mode that you play  this is gonna teach you how to enter  certain fights with your troops how to  tell them to come towards you how to  defend how to attack what different  units are how they fare against other  units what formations you want them to  be placed down in and other things like  that to help you succeed the troops of  themselves also have a unit tree to  upgrade them for more damage and more  skills as well which is really cool so  lots of diversity in those specific  units I was going up against guys whose  minions and troops were on horseback so  that can definitely be a problem if I  was going up against those guys luckily  they were on my team the other trainings  also consist of siege attack training  and siege defense training while also  understanding how to use some of the new  mechanics within the battle like the  troop selection basically you can walk  up in the middle of a PvP game and go to  the troop section and swap out troops as  you need to let's say maybe that this  isn't the correct way maybe you don't  want to be using archers in this  situation you want to be using some  short-range people you could swap out  but obviously they're not everywhere in  the map they're very close to your spawn  it does have that negative aspect of you  having to go back to base roughly to go  get your troops you can't just do it  wherever and you'd be just sitting there  for the whole game these trainings like  the siege attack and the siege defense  will become available to you as you  progress through the story and play the  different game modes you're first gonna  be able to play training camp and then  once you win a game in training camp you  go to field battle and before you play  field battle it teaches you some of the  mechanics like capping objectives and  then you go to siege battle and of  course before siege battle you learn  about the  attacking and defending and then you go  on to death match and then you continue  after that up into other high level  things like expeditions and territory  Wars some of the expeditions the minimum  is level 20 with the expedition 3 being  a minimum rank of level 60 so especially  at 62 my knowledge is the highest rank  that you can get to so lots of levels to  use and you can use those level ups to  either auto assign or pick yourself and  upgrade your abilities with doing more  damage having more health other stuff  like that to help you in your PvP  matches I chose auto assigned since I  wasn't really familiar with what I  wanted to do with my character but if  you know exactly how you want to play it  you can obviously pick it on your own  stats now we can finally get into the  multiplayer side and this is definitely  one of my favorite things about this  game it seems like it is the main core  of the game and it's obviously really  well done and is definitely my favorite  what you do as soon as you start the  game as you pick the weapon you want  then you pick your equipment like siege  weapons and then you also select your  troops that you want to follow with you  into battle like I said before you can  swap these out whenever you want or when  that unit dies you can pick up a new  unit but this is for when you want to  pick the very first one you want to drop  with I usually end up picking the  pikemen as my very first choice because  for at least to me these things are  absolutely busted you want to fight  these minions in these troops like you  would if you're playing a MOBA obviously  if you're playing MOBAs like League of  Legends and smite you don't want to go  up against a group of minions when  you're on your own you want to have your  own minions fight them and you kind of  dish damage in the background while  avoiding hits this is kind of the same  premise you don't want to fight an  entire group of troops they will  absolutely melt you as they're seeing on  screen I killed like three or four guys  just using the pikemen because these  guys decided to pick archers even if  they had melee attack troopers they were  too far back and they didn't catch up to  him leaving them completely vulnerable  and they were melted in a couple seconds  now personally I didn't get a chance to  use every single weapon in every single  skill within those weapons that would  just take way too long to do and it  would take a hell of a lot of grinding  and time that I don't have to do so but  I know at least for the dual blades that  have some sort of smoke bomb you can  throw on to the ground and it  incapacitate the opponent for a little  bit and if you could find one of those  abilities to use on any of those weapons  that will help tremendously I know one  of the boys has like a kick that does  the same thing it leaves the opponent  knocked back for a couple seconds and  then you can end up using combos and  then like  said prepare that what the pikemen  you're gonna be destroying these guys in  one to two seconds if you're sick of  doing PvP battles and want to have some  kind of meaning to your fights of course  you can always do territory Wars you can  do that by joining a house and/or  Alliance and you can join up with those  do a bunch of territory Wars fight for  your Alliance and claim different areas  on the map which is always really cool  currently right now there is two things  going on there is season two which  dropped I think about a month or two ago  and they have a brand new unit called  the son of steps which is inspired by  the Mongolian warrior so if you end up  getting to that point you can use them  there's also a new battle pass with a  set of new challenges you could score  some season exclusive nomadic themes as  well as three new battlefields are gonna  be available to play and then the new  season also introduces more content  improvements matchmaking features UI  changes more NPC houses a new ranking  system player titles and a load more the  second thing that also went live at the  time that I'm making this at is actually  live right now on January 23rd is  actually the Lunar New Year it has a  bunch of different things going on right  now with different cosmetics and items  that you can pick up throughout the next  couple weeks so this is definitely a  perfect time to hop into the game and  get those rewards overall I gotta say  though this is definitely a really fun  game a lot better than I was expecting  it to be has some really nice unique  elements that I've never really seen in  a lot of games before and all of those  elements the MMO side with the PvE in  the PvP content and that real-time  strategy they all kind of meshed  together and flow really well into this  really cool multiplayer game one thing I  noticed though when playing PvP some of  the guys that were extremely high  leveled were actually kicking my ass  because of their really good minions so  to help you guys out you can click the  link down in the description to get a  bunch of different troops that I didn't  have access to but then you can have  access to so you don't have to have this  problem that I did and you can breeze  through the competition as always thank  you to conquerors blade for sponsoring  today's video but with that guys like  the video if you do enjoy subscriber for  you click the link down in the  description and in the comments for all  the juicy stuff on how to download  conquers blade and everything with it  and take care guys I'll see you in the  next video peace out  [Music]

